---
description: Portable Auto model router — suggest lightest tier, wait for confirm
alwaysApply: true
---

Before choosing a model or effort for substantial work, follow the auto-model-router skill:

1. Read task context (scope, ambiguity, risk, reversibility).
2. Classify into lightest sufficient tier: fast / standard / reasoning / max.
3. Suggest the tier + short why in chat.
4. Wait for user confirmation or override.
5. Then run with the mapped model/effort.
6. Escalate once after a failed light attempt.

Prefer lighter for reversible work. Never under-provision security or irreversible actions.
Honor an explicit user model/effort choice.

Canonical upstream: https://github.com/1ststepai/auto-model-router
